cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PerioRisk in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "PerioRisk: periodontitis risk screening from self-reported questions"
abstract: >-
  PerioRisk estimates the probability of moderate or severe periodontitis (CDC/AAP surveillance case
  definition) from 14 self-reported questions. A calibrated gradient-boosting model was developed on
  NHANES 2009-2012 (n = 7,050) and temporally validated on NHANES 2013-2014 (n = 3,610; AUC 0.781,
  95% CI 0.766-0.796; calibration slope 0.91), with decision-curve, subgroup and survey-weighted
  analyses reported following TRIPOD+AI. The fitted model is exported to a portable JSON format and
  re-implemented in pure Python and JavaScript, reproducing scikit-learn's predictions to within
  1e-12, and ships as a dependency-free Python package, a command-line tool and a private
  in-browser application. The pipeline reproduces the published model exactly from public data.
